### Colonial Empire JE widget — the player-facing surface for je_colonial_empire,
### laid out to docs/guides/gui_style_guide.md.
###
### Three roots at the foot of this file, all mounted from je_colonial_empire:
###   widget_je_colonial_empire_overview   custom_widget_container_1
###       the overview (te_ce_overview_panel), always shown: the band, the
###       programmes running, the stability bar with where it is heading and
###       a line where the next band begins, the completion clocks in the top
###       band, and the condemning and supporting great powers' shares of
###       prestige.
###   widget_je_colonial_empire_status     custom_widget_container_2
###       te_ce_status_sections, open: why stability is moving (pillar bars,
###       and the eligible territories as a collapsed list), international
###       pressure, the three colonial programmes, the three decolonization
###       decisions.
###   widget_je_colonial_empire_reference  custom_widget_container_3
###       te_ce_reference_sections: the two history charts, then "How the
###       Colonial Empire Works", the one collapsed section of explanations.
### The overview draws the stability bar, so the entry also attaches
### te_je_bars_on_top_marker to custom_widget_container_7 and the journal panel
### drops its own bar at the bottom (gui/journal_entry.gui; je_banking.txt).
###
### Every section is a type (te_ce_sec_*) and the two composers set their order,
### so a system tab can instance the same pieces later (style rule 9). The
### roots are thin wrappers that repeat the composers' IsActive gate.
###
### Collapse flags say their default: *_closed sections are open until closed,
### *_open ones collapsed until opened (test_colonial_empire_layout.py).
###
### The vanilla button grid is AI-only (`is_ai = yes` on the three decision
### buttons) and the programmes have no buttons (the AI steps them in the
### entry's monthly pulse), so every action a human could take has a control
### here. Each control calls the SAME shared trigger/effect the AI uses, through
### common/scripted_guis/colonial_empire_sguis.txt.
###
### OP TABLE — colonial_empire_policy_sgui
###   0  raise Development Investment      1  lower Development Investment
###   2  raise Military Garrison           3  lower Military Garrison
###   4  raise Cultural Assimilation       5  lower Cultural Assimilation
###
### OP TABLE — colonial_empire_decision_sgui
###   0  Release a Colonial Territory   1  Planned Full Decolonization
###   2  Round Table Conference
###
### Both tables are repeated in the sgui file and in
### docs/systems/journal_entry_systems.md § Colonial Stability Widget. Keep all
### three in step.
###
### An op code decides what a control DOES, never whether it is DRAWN. Each
### programme's minus and plus are always drawn and grey out through IsValid.
### The overview's lit and dimmed programme icons take their visibility from a
### scope-free read-only handler — colonial_empire_active_{invest,garrison,assimilation}_sgui
### — lit on `IsShown(...)`, dimmed on `Not(IsShown(...))`. Passing a saved
### scope to IsValid / Execute / the tooltips is proven in this mod; passing one
### to IsShown is not, and with the button grid hidden from humans a control
### whose visibility quietly evaluated false would leave no control at all. The
### sgui file header has the full reasoning. Do not move visibility onto an
### op-parameterised IsShown.
###
### NO NUMBER IS TYPED IN THIS FILE. The nine stability contributions come from
### colonial_stability_drift_* script values — the same leaves the bar itself
### consumes — six read live and three read from the snapshot variables
### colonial_empire_refresh_display writes; each pillar bar's range is a
### colonial_pillar_* script value. The eligible territories are the states
### colonial_empire_refresh_display stores (colonial_empire_territory_1..8),
### each read through colonial_territory_disp_* values that call the entry's
### own triggers. The band and the next band's edge
### come from the live band ladder (colonial_empire_live_tier /
### colonial_empire_live_next_boundary in colonial_empire_values.txt), never
### from the snapshot, which is stale on a newly activated entry; the overview
### reads them and its snapshots through the guarded colonial_empire_disp_*
### values.
### Programme effects come from [GetStaticModifier('x').GetDesc], and their
### levels, costs and bar terms from the PROGRAMME LEVELS / PROGRAMME COSTS
### script values in colonial_empire_values.txt (all O(1); the colonies' GDP is
### cached monthly). If you need a new number here, derive it there or in
### colonial_empire_display_effects.txt and read it.
###
### je_colonial_empire carries `is_shown_when_inactive`, so every root is gated
### on [JournalEntry.IsActive] (gotcha #14: an unguarded display sgui in that
### state produces a "Failed to fetch variable" per frame for every country that
### can merely see the entry). Inside, every var read is additionally gated on
### colonial_empire_display_ready, which asks script whether
### colonial_empire_refresh_display has run yet.
###
### Section open/closed state and the chart range live in GetVariableSystem —
### client-side UI state, never saved, never gameplay state. There is no armed
### action state anywhere: the three decolonization decisions confirm through
### decolonization_events.400 / .401, which is real game state and offers a
### Reconsider option.
###
### Art: the band, alert and programme icons, the pie's three discs and the
### territory list's colony icon are the system's own, in
### gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/ (PR #586). Each is listed, with
### what it shows, in docs/systems/colonial_empire_gui_icons.md. The trend
### arrows, the pie's round frame and the bar's line are vanilla's.

types colonial_empire_widget_types
{
	type colonial_empire_text = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_large
	}

	type colonial_empire_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		margin = { 20 8 }

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_fancy_dark
			alpha = 0.5
		}
	}

	type colonial_empire_section_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			parentanchor = hcenter
			size = { 520 38 }
		}
		blockoverride "left_text_alignment" {
			align = left|nobaseline
		}
	}

	### A heading inside a section's panel, over one group of its lines, with a
	### faint rule under it (un_chamber_subheader's shape).
	type colonial_empire_subheader = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 1
		block "subheader_margin" {
			margin_top = 10
		}

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_large
			default_format = "#title"
			block "subheader_text" {}
		}
		divider_clean = {
			blockoverride "size" {
				size = { 480 2 }
			}
		}
	}

	### Explanatory text under a subheading in "How the Colonial Empire Works":
	### how a part of the system works, rather than what it says now.
	type colonial_empire_note = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_medium
		default_format = "#lore"
	}

	### A line of the eligible-territories list (its caption, and the lines
	### for none and for not yet assessed): the medium font, the rows' width.
	type colonial_empire_list_text = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 476 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 476 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_medium
	}

	### A table row: a label on the left and its value on the right
	### (un_chamber_value_row's shape). Every row carries a tooltip with the
	### reason behind its value, so the label is marked hoverable. 250 + 210:
	### the value column holds the longest state name, "South Atlantic
	### Islands" (22 characters, about 208 units in the medium font), for the
	### Decolonization section's "Largest" row (play-test round 3's width
	### budget; it was 320 + 140).
	type colonial_empire_value_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		margin = { 4 1 }

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 250 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 250 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			elide = right
			block "row_label" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 210 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 210 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#v"
			elide = right
			block "row_value" {}
		}
	}

	### One term of the bar's formula as a pillar, the UN's "why authority is
	### moving" rows (un_authority_widget.gui): its name, a double bar and its
	### signed value. The bar is vanilla's double_direction_progressbar, zero
	### at the centre line, the negative half red from the left and the
	### positive half green to the right. Each half is a 0-1 fraction of the
	### term's own range (colonial_pillar_* in colonial_empire_values.txt,
	### clamped there), so a term past its range fills its half and the value
	### beside it still reads true. A row with no bar (the base decline, the
	### monthly limit, the projected change) leaves the bar's cell empty, so
	### every value sits in one column. Fixed cells, 190 + 190 + 72, two 8 px
	### gaps and the margins = 476: the longest label, "Great Power pressure",
	### is 20 characters, about 189 units in the medium font.
	type colonial_empire_pillar_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 8
		margin = { 4 1 }

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 190 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 190 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			elide = right
			block "row_label" {}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 190 14 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			block "row_bar" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 72 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 72 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#v"
			elide = right
			block "row_value" {}
		}
	}

	### An expandable list nested inside a section's panel, set in from the
	### panel's edge by the flowcontainer that holds it (un_chamber_subsection_header's
	### shape, copied rather than instanced so this file does not depend on the
	### UN's).
	type colonial_empire_subsection_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			size = { 440 30 }
		}
		blockoverride "fontsize" {
			using = fontsize_medium
		}
		blockoverride "arrow_size" {
			size = { 20 20 }
		}
		blockoverride "left_textbox_margin_left" {
			margin_left = 32
		}
	}

	### The eligible-territories list: its column heads, then one row per
	### stored territory. Fixed cells, 24 + 210 + 58 + 56 + 40 + 68 and five
	### 4 px gaps = 476, so a long name cannot widen the row: the longest state
	### name, "South Atlantic Islands", is 22 characters, about 208 units in
	### the medium font. The heads are in the small font ("Primary", 7
	### characters, about 54 units).
	type te_ce_territory_head = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		spacing = 4
		ignoreinvisible = yes

		widget = {
			size = { 24 20 }
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 210 20 }
			textbox = {
				parentanchor = left|vcenter
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 210
				elide = right
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_small
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "je_colonial_empire_territory_head_name"
				tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_head_name_tt"
			}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 58 20 }
			textbox = {
				parentanchor = right|vcenter
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 58
				elide = right
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_small
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "je_colonial_empire_territory_head_pop"
				tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_head_pop_tt"
			}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 56 20 }
			textbox = {
				parentanchor = right|vcenter
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 56
				elide = right
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_small
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "je_colonial_empire_territory_head_primary"
				tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_head_primary_tt"
			}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 40 20 }
			textbox = {
				parentanchor = right|vcenter
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 40
				elide = right
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_small
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "je_colonial_empire_territory_head_sol"
				tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_head_sol_tt"
			}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 68 20 }
			textbox = {
				parentanchor = right|vcenter
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 68
				elide = right
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_small
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "je_colonial_empire_territory_head_gdp"
				tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_head_gdp_tt"
			}
		}
	}

	### One territory: whether it counts as a colony (the colony icon lit, or
	### dimmed), its name, people, primary-culture share, standard of living
	### and GDP, in te_ce_territory_head's cells. The share is red while the
	### indigenous-population test holds, the standard of living red while the
	### living-standards test holds: the figure that makes it a colony. Each
	### cell's hover gives the figure's threshold.
	###
	### The instance gates the row on the count of stored rows ("row_visible")
	### and sets the stored state as its datacontext ("row_context"), on the
	### inner container so the variable is read only while the row is shown
	### (Space Race's rival rows). Every cell reads the state through
	### State.MakeScope.ScriptValue (grand monuments' rows), the
	### colonial_territory_disp_* values that call the entry's own triggers.
	type te_ce_territory_row = widget {
		size = { 476 24 }
		block "row_visible" {}

		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			spacing = 4
			parentanchor = vcenter
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			block "row_context" {}

			widget = {
				size = { 24 24 }
				parentanchor = vcenter

				icon = {
					size = { 22 22 }
					parentanchor = center
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( State.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_territory_disp_colony'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/territory_colony.dds"
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_colony_tt"
				}
				icon = {
					size = { 22 22 }
					parentanchor = center
					alpha = 0.25
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( State.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_territory_disp_colony'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/territory_colony.dds"
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_not_colony_tt"
				}
			}
			widget = {
				size = { 210 24 }
				parentanchor = vcenter

				textbox = {
					parentanchor = left|vcenter
					autoresize = yes
					max_width = 210
					elide = right
					align = left|nobaseline
					using = fontsize_medium
					text = "[State.GetName]"
				}
			}
			widget = {
				size = { 58 24 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_pop_tt"

				textbox = {
					parentanchor = right|vcenter
					autoresize = yes
					max_width = 58
					elide = right
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = fontsize_medium
					text = "je_colonial_empire_territory_pop"
				}
			}
			widget = {
				size = { 56 24 }
				parentanchor = vcenter

				textbox = {
					parentanchor = right|vcenter
					autoresize = yes
					max_width = 56
					elide = right
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = fontsize_medium
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( State.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_territory_disp_indigenous'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
					text = "je_colonial_empire_territory_primary_bad"
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_primary_bad_tt"
				}
				textbox = {
					parentanchor = right|vcenter
					autoresize = yes
					max_width = 56
					elide = right
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = fontsize_medium
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( State.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_territory_disp_indigenous'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
					text = "je_colonial_empire_territory_primary"
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_primary_tt"
				}
			}
			widget = {
				size = { 40 24 }
				parentanchor = vcenter

				textbox = {
					parentanchor = right|vcenter
					autoresize = yes
					max_width = 40
					elide = right
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = fontsize_medium
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( State.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_territory_disp_disparity'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
					text = "je_colonial_empire_territory_sol_bad"
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_sol_bad_tt"
				}
				textbox = {
					parentanchor = right|vcenter
					autoresize = yes
					max_width = 40
					elide = right
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = fontsize_medium
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( State.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_territory_disp_disparity'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
					text = "je_colonial_empire_territory_sol"
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_sol_tt"
				}
			}
			widget = {
				size = { 68 24 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_territory_gdp_tt"

				textbox = {
					parentanchor = right|vcenter
					autoresize = yes
					max_width = 68
					elide = right
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = fontsize_medium
					text = "je_colonial_empire_territory_gdp"
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### One programme: its name and costs on the left, its level, and a minus
	### and a plus that step it down and up (op codes: the table in this file's
	### header). Both controls are always drawn; a step that cannot be taken
	### greys out with the reason in its tooltip (IsValidTooltip, then what the
	### step does). Both address colonial_empire_policy_sgui, so the
	### datacontext lives on the type and each row passes its two op codes.
	type colonial_empire_policy_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 6
		margin = { 4 4 }
		parentanchor = hcenter
		datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_policy_sgui')]"

		flowcontainer = {
			direction = vertical
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			parentanchor = vcenter
			minimumsize = { 360 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 360 -1 }

			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				multiline = yes
				minimumsize = { 360 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 360 -1 }
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_medium
				block "row_label" {}
			}
			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				multiline = yes
				minimumsize = { 360 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 360 -1 }
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_small
				block "row_cost" {}
			}
		}

		widget = {
			size = { 50 26 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			textbox = {
				parentanchor = center
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 50
				elide = right
				align = center|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_medium
				block "row_level" {}
			}
		}

		widget = {
			size = { 76 28 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			flowcontainer = {
				parentanchor = center
				direction = horizontal
				spacing = 12

				button_icon_minus_action = {
					size = { 26 26 }
					parentanchor = vcenter
					block "down_action" {}
				}
				button_icon_plus_action = {
					size = { 26 26 }
					parentanchor = vcenter
					block "up_action" {}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### One decolonization decision: its name on the left, what it does on
	### hover, and the control that opens its confirmation event beside it
	### (style rule 6; it used to sit under a paragraph, flush left). Every row
	### shares one scripted GUI and differs only by op code, so the datacontext
	### lives here.
	type colonial_empire_decision_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 10
		margin = { 4 4 }
		datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_decision_sgui')]"

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			minimumsize = { 300 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 300 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "row_text" {}
		}

		button = {
			using = default_button_action
			size = { 150 28 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			textbox = {
				parentanchor = center
				align = center|nobaseline
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 140
				elide = right
				using = fontsize_small
				text = "je_colonial_empire_btn_open_choice"
			}

			block "row_action" {}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### OVERVIEW. Always shown, not collapsible (style rule 1).
	### ======================================================================

	### A cell of the overview: an icon, its word small beneath. Fixed width,
	### so a long word cannot push the row wider (te_un_ov_icon_label's shape).
	type te_ce_ov_icon_label = widget {
		size = { 110 58 }

		icon = {
			size = { 36 36 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			block "icon_texture" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			parentanchor = bottom|hcenter
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 108
			elide = right
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_small
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "label" {}
		}
	}

	### One programme: full colour while it runs, dimmed while it does not. The
	### instance sets the texture on both icons, and the visible gate and
	### tooltip on each (te_un_ov_agency's shape).
	type te_ce_ov_programme = widget {
		size = { 40 40 }

		icon = {
			size = { 36 36 }
			parentanchor = center
			block "lit" {}
			block "programme_texture" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 36 36 }
			parentanchor = center
			alpha = 0.25
			block "unlit" {}
			block "programme_texture" {}
		}
	}

	### Great-power prestige as a pie: the condemners' share and, beside it in
	### its own colour, the supporters' share, over a background disc inside
	### vanilla's decorated round frame (te_un_ov_pie's shape; the recipe is
	### "Pie charts of script-held data" in gui_modding_guide.md). Stacked
	### largest first: the supporters' layer fills to the sum of both shares
	### and the condemners' layer on top to its own, so each shows as its own
	### slice. Frame 1 of each texture is transparent, frame 2 the colour. The
	### legend beside it names the slices (te_ce_ov_legend_row).
	type te_ce_ov_pie = widget {
		size = { 86 86 }

		icon = {
			size = { 86 86 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/round_frame_dec.dds"
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 62 62 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			position = { 0 12 }

			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				value = 1
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/pie_rest.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "pie_value_cum" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/pie_supporters.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "pie_value" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/pie_condemners.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
		}
	}

	### One line of the pie's legend: its slice's texture as a swatch (frame 2
	### is the coloured disc, as in ch_model_legend_row) and the share.
	type te_ce_ov_legend_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 6

		icon = {
			size = { 14 14 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			framesize = { 128 128 }
			frame = 2
			block "legend_swatch" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 180
			elide = right
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			block "legend_text" {}
		}
	}

	### What a returning player checks: which band, which programmes are
	### running, where the bar is and which way it is moving, how close the
	### empire is to winning once it is Solidified, and how much of the great
	### powers' weight condemns or backs us.
	type te_ce_overview_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		colonial_empire_panel = {
			### Pinned to the 480 column. A frame whose width comes from its content
			### is centred by the width it had at first layout, and the pressure
			### alert and the completion clocks appear later, behind their gates
			### (Nuclear and Global Warming drew off-centre until pinned, play-test
			### 2026-09-29).
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				spacing = 10
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 480 -1 }

				### Before the first monthly assessment (a save upgraded mid-entry):
				### one line in place of the rows that read the snapshot.
				colonial_empire_text = {
					visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
					text = "je_colonial_empire_conditions_pending"
				}

				### Row 1: the band · the programmes running
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = horizontal
					spacing = 6
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					parentanchor = hcenter

					### The band. Its tooltip is the entry's status line and the
					### modifier the band puts on the entry (the panel's old "While in
					### this band" line).
					flowcontainer = {
						ignoreinvisible = yes
						visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
						tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_band_tt"

						te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_tier'), '(CFixedPoint)5' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/band_solidified.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "je_colonial_empire_band_solidified"
							}
						}
						te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_tier'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/band_stable.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "je_colonial_empire_band_stable"
							}
						}
						te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_tier'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/band_strained.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "je_colonial_empire_band_strained"
							}
						}
						te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_tier'), '(CFixedPoint)2' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/band_crumbling.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "je_colonial_empire_band_crumbling"
							}
						}
						te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_tier'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/band_collapsing.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "je_colonial_empire_band_collapsing"
							}
						}
					}

					### The three programmes, lit while they run. Which half of each
					### pair is drawn comes from the same scope-free handlers that pick
					### the Enable or the Disable control below.
					widget = {
						size = { 150 58 }

						flowcontainer = {
							direction = horizontal
							spacing = 4
							parentanchor = top|hcenter

							te_ce_ov_programme = {
								blockoverride "programme_texture" {
									texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/programme_invest.dds"
								}
								blockoverride "lit" {
									visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_invest_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
									tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_invest_on_tt"
								}
								blockoverride "unlit" {
									visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_invest_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
									tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_invest_off_tt"
								}
							}
							te_ce_ov_programme = {
								blockoverride "programme_texture" {
									texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/programme_garrison.dds"
								}
								blockoverride "lit" {
									visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_garrison_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
									tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_garrison_on_tt"
								}
								blockoverride "unlit" {
									visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_garrison_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
									tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_garrison_off_tt"
								}
							}
							te_ce_ov_programme = {
								blockoverride "programme_texture" {
									texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/programme_assimilation.dds"
								}
								blockoverride "lit" {
									visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_assimilation_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
									tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_assimilation_on_tt"
								}
								blockoverride "unlit" {
									visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_assimilation_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
									tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_assimilation_off_tt"
								}
							}
						}
						textbox = {
							parentanchor = bottom|hcenter
							autoresize = yes
							align = hcenter|nobaseline
							using = fontsize_small
							text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_programmes_label"
						}
					}
				}

				### Row 2: the stability bar, where it is heading, a line where the
				### next band begins, the value and this month's projected change, and
				### its direction. Reached the way vanilla's journal panel reaches it,
				### through the entry's own datamodel (one scripted bar, so one item).
				### The row's tooltip is the engine's own term-by-term breakdown, which
				### reads only the ScriptedProgressBar. Gotcha #24: a tooltip in a
				### datamodel item has no JournalEntry, so the value's and the line's
				### own hovers read GetPlayer (the entry's owner: a player sees only
				### his own journal). Everything else in the row is a widget property or
				### text, which does see JournalEntry. Four fixed cells, 90 + 180 + 145
				### + 24 and three 8 px gaps = 463: "100% (-1.67/mo)" is 15 characters,
				### about 142 units (it elided in 120, play-test round 3).
				###
				### THE BAR (play-test round 3, 2026-09-30; the Global Warming bar's
				### construction, e4db4ce9). Five layers in one fixed 180 x 18 cell,
				### bottom to top, so the solid fill is always the lower of today's
				### stability and where it is heading, and the translucent stretch runs
				### to the higher:
				###   1. default_progressbar_horizontal at value 0: the bar's own
				###      background and frame, no fill.
				###   2. Rising (colonial_empire_disp_trend 1): green_progressbar_horizontal's
				###      fill at 40% (a wrapper widget, alpha = 0.4), blanked, up to the
				###      higher value, where the bar is heading. Green because rising
				###      stability is good for the player.
				###   3. Falling (colonial_empire_disp_trend -1): bad_progressbar_horizontal's
				###      red fill at 50%, blanked, up to the higher value, today's: the
				###      stretch about to be lost. Red because falling is bad.
				###   4. default_progressbar_horizontal's own fill, background and frame
				###      blanked, up to the lower of the two: solid.
				###   5. The next band's edge as a thin 3 px cream line (a progressbar
				###      marker drawn with white.dds tinted by `color`), with its own
				###      hover. In bands 1-4 only (colonial_empire_disp_next_tick): in
				###      the top band the edge is the bar's end, which the completion
				###      clocks below count toward.
				### "Where it is heading" is stability in colonial_empire_projection_months
				### (12) at this month's projected change (colonial_empire_disp_projected),
				### and today's value is colonial_empire_live_bar, the bar read as a whole
				### number. No eye marker.
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = vertical
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					parentanchor = hcenter
					datamodel = "[JournalEntry.GetScriptedProgressBars]"

					item = {
						flowcontainer = {
							direction = horizontal
							spacing = 8
							ignoreinvisible = yes
							tooltip = "[ScriptedProgressBar.GetPeriodicProgressBreakdown]"

							textbox = {
								minimumsize = { 90 -1 }
								maximumsize = { 90 -1 }
								autoresize = yes
								parentanchor = vcenter
								align = left|nobaseline
								elide = right
								text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_stability_label"
							}
							widget = {
								size = { 180 18 }
								parentanchor = vcenter

								# 1. Background and frame.
								default_progressbar_horizontal = {
									size = { 100% 100% }
									blockoverride "values" {
										value = 0
										min = 0
										max = 1
									}
								}
								# 2. Rising, good: the green stretch to where it is heading.
								widget = {
									size = { 100% 100% }
									alpha = 0.4
									visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_trend'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"

									green_progressbar_horizontal = {
										size = { 100% 100% }
										blockoverride "background" {}
										blockoverride "frame" {}
										blockoverride "values" {
											value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_bar_high_frac') )]"
											min = 0
											max = 1
										}
									}
								}
								# 3. Falling, bad: the red stretch from where it is heading up to today.
								widget = {
									size = { 100% 100% }
									alpha = 0.5
									visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_trend'), '(CFixedPoint)-1' )]"

									bad_progressbar_horizontal = {
										size = { 100% 100% }
										blockoverride "background" {}
										blockoverride "frame" {}
										blockoverride "values" {
											value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_bar_high_frac') )]"
											min = 0
											max = 1
										}
									}
								}
								# 4. Solid: the lower of today and where it is heading.
								default_progressbar_horizontal = {
									size = { 100% 100% }
									blockoverride "background" {}
									blockoverride "frame" {}
									blockoverride "values" {
										value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_bar_low_frac') )]"
										min = 0
										max = 1
									}
								}
								# 5. The next band's edge: a thin line with its own hover.
								progressbar = {
									visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_next_tick'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
									noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
									progresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
									size = { 100% 100% }
									skip_initial_animation = yes
									direction = horizontal
									value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_next_boundary_frac') )]"
									min = 0
									max = 1
									marker = {
										icon = {
											size = { 3 24 }
											parentanchor = vcenter
											widgetanchor = center
											texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
											color = { 0.96 0.90 0.72 0.95 }
											tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_tick_tt"
										}
									}
								}
							}
							textbox = {
								minimumsize = { 145 -1 }
								maximumsize = { 145 -1 }
								autoresize = yes
								parentanchor = vcenter
								align = left|nobaseline
								default_format = "#tooltippable"
								elide = right
								text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_stability_value"
								tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_heading_tt"
							}
							widget = {
								size = { 24 24 }
								parentanchor = vcenter

								icon = {
									size = { 24 24 }
									visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_trend'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
									texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_up.dds"
								}
								icon = {
									size = { 24 24 }
									visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_trend'), '(CFixedPoint)-1' )]"
									texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_down.dds"
								}
								icon = {
									size = { 24 24 }
									visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_trend'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
									texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_nochange.dds"
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}

				### Row 3: where the next band begins, under the line that marks it.
				textbox = {
					visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
					autoresize = yes
					parentanchor = hcenter
					align = hcenter|nobaseline
					using = fontsize_medium
					text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_next"
				}

				### Row 4, in the top band only: the completion clocks, each a bar whose
				### end is its target. Months held at 100 against
				### colonial_empire_completion_months, the count je_colonial_empire's
				### `complete` reads; and, for a great power, the months Solidified against
				### colonial_empire_federation_months, the Imperial Federation Act's gate.
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = vertical
					spacing = 4
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					parentanchor = hcenter
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_tier'), '(CFixedPoint)5' )]"

					flowcontainer = {
						direction = vertical
						spacing = 2
						parentanchor = hcenter
						tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_hold_tt"

						textbox = {
							autoresize = yes
							parentanchor = hcenter
							align = hcenter|nobaseline
							using = fontsize_medium
							default_format = "#tooltippable"
							text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_hold"
						}
						default_progressbar_horizontal = {
							size = { 240 12 }
							parentanchor = hcenter
							blockoverride "values" {
								value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_at_100_frac') )]"
								min = 0
								max = 1
							}
						}
					}
					flowcontainer = {
						direction = vertical
						spacing = 2
						parentanchor = hcenter
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_act_in_reach'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
						tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_act_tt"

						textbox = {
							autoresize = yes
							parentanchor = hcenter
							align = hcenter|nobaseline
							using = fontsize_medium
							default_format = "#tooltippable"
							text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_act"
						}
						default_progressbar_horizontal = {
							size = { 240 12 }
							parentanchor = hcenter
							blockoverride "values" {
								value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_solidified_frac') )]"
								min = 0
								max = 1
							}
						}
					}
				}

				### Row 5: the great powers. The pie is great-power prestige (ours
				### included): the condemners' share, the number the two escalations fire
				### on, and the supporters' share in its own colour, which no escalation
				### reads. The legend says so. The group's tooltip is International
				### Pressure's roster. Beside it, the escalation in force, if any.
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = horizontal
					spacing = 6
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					parentanchor = hcenter
					visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"

					flowcontainer = {
						direction = horizontal
						spacing = 8
						ignoreinvisible = yes
						tooltip = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_pressure_sgui').ExecuteTooltip(GuiScope.SetRoot(JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope).End)]"

						te_ce_ov_pie = {
							parentanchor = vcenter
							blockoverride "pie_value_cum" {
								value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_pressure_cum') )]"
							}
							blockoverride "pie_value" {
								value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_condemner_share') )]"
							}
						}
						flowcontainer = {
							direction = vertical
							spacing = 2
							ignoreinvisible = yes
							parentanchor = vcenter
							minimumsize = { 200 -1 }
							maximumsize = { 200 -1 }

							te_ce_ov_legend_row = {
								blockoverride "legend_swatch" {
									texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/pie_condemners.dds"
								}
								blockoverride "legend_text" {
									text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_legend_condemn"
								}
							}
							te_ce_ov_legend_row = {
								blockoverride "legend_swatch" {
									texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/pie_supporters.dds"
								}
								blockoverride "legend_text" {
									text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_legend_support"
								}
							}
							textbox = {
								autoresize = yes
								multiline = yes
								minimumsize = { 200 -1 }
								maximumsize = { 200 -1 }
								align = left|nobaseline
								using = fontsize_small
								text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_legend_note"
							}
						}
					}
					te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_pressure_level'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
						parentanchor = vcenter
						tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_isolation_tt"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/alert_isolation.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_isolation"
						}
					}
					te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_pressure_level'), '(CFixedPoint)2' )]"
						parentanchor = vcenter
						tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_consensus_tt"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/colonial_empire_icons/alert_consensus.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_consensus"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### SECTIONS. Each is composed, in order, by te_ce_status_sections or
	### te_ce_reference_sections below.
	### ======================================================================

	### Why stability is moving: the terms of the bar's formula as pillar bars
	### (colonial_empire_pillar_row, the UN's "why authority is moving" rows;
	### play-test round 3), then the monthly limit and the total, then the
	### eligible territories as a list. Open by default (the CLOSED flag). Each
	### row's tooltip says what the term holds; the explanations are in "How
	### the Colonial Empire Works".
	type te_ce_sec_stability = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		colonial_empire_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_stability_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('colonial_empire_stability_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_stability_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_stability_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		colonial_empire_panel = {
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_stability_closed'))]"

			# Shown for a save upgraded mid-entry, until the first pulse.
			colonial_empire_text = {
				visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
				text = "je_colonial_empire_conditions_pending"
			}

			# Six terms read live (a click moves them the next frame); the
			# three that iterate — overreach, great-power pressure, acceptance —
			# read this month's snapshot, behind the display_ready gate. Each bar
			# spans its term's range (colonial_pillar_* in
			# colonial_empire_values.txt, where each range's derivation is noted).
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"

				# A constant, so no bar.
				colonial_empire_pillar_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_base_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_base"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_stability_drift_base')|=+2]"
					}
				}
